tatement_sha256":"sha256:9431b0bdca257f58cb9182938298e3575540f2e72853c8b8da8644fc58183abc","file":"preprints/Uniform-quasipolynomial-time-trace-reconstruction-October-5-2026/build/manuscript/main.tex","line":78,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"98270c13f12cbf6dd8bef238a94e37202879a795b84be9f6b5ebb34f67021f3b","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Uniform-quasipolynomial-time-trace-reconstruction-October-5-2026/build/manuscript/main.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:9431b0bdca257f58cb9182938298e3575540f2e72853c8b8da8644fc58183abc","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Uniform-quasipolynomial-time-trace-reconstruction-October-5-2026/build/manuscript/main.tex#L78"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere exist absolute constants $C,c\\ge1$ and one randomized multitape\nTuring machine $\\mathcal A$ with the following property. For every\n$n\\ge2$, every rational $p\\in(0,1]$, and every $x\\in\\{0,1\\}^n$, given\n$n,p$ in binary and access to independent ordinary deletion traces of\n$x$, the machine requests at most\n\\[\n M_C(n,p)=\\left\\lceil\\exp\\bigl(CB(n,p)\\bigr)\\right\\rceil\n\\]\ntraces, outputs an element of $\\{0,1\\}^n$, and returns $x$ with probability\nat least $2/3$.\n\nFor every internal random-bit sequence and every well-formed trace\nstream of strings of length at most $n$, it halts within\n\\[\n \\bigl(n+L+M_C(n,p)\\bigr)^c\n\\]\nbit operations. This bound includes preprocessing, all parameter and\nfinite-precision calculations, every received trace bit and delimiter,\nand the output. The only oracle operation is the external generation\nof the independent deletion traces."}
